Peter wrote:
> Are the properties of healthstones linearly cumulative? Are 5
> healthstones 5 times better than 1 healthstone? Is there an absolute
> effectiveness cutoff?
>
> The world must know.

>From http://www.statslab.cam.ac.uk/~eva/slashem/stones.html :

Healthstones affect the rate at which you heal. Blessed or uncursed
healthstones increase it, cursed healthstones decrease it, and
unfortunately healthstones are always generated cursed. Unlike
luckstones, healthstones are cumulative - two blessed healthstones are
better than one. To be precise, you have a health bonus which is 2 for
each blessed healthstone in you main inventory, plus 1 for each
uncursed healthstone, minus 2 for each cursed healthstone. This bonus
is added to your level and constitution when calculating how fast you
heal.



